Subject: [PATCH] chore(geno-audit): bring geno-dev into ecosystem compliance

- S4: add allowed-tools to root SKILL.md frontmatter
- S5/S6: add geno-dev-sessions-remote to GENO.md skills table
- S6: add versioning guidance to GENO.md Conventions section
- S11: remove /gt-pr alias from geno-dev-prs-check SKILL.md description
Note: geno-dev-sessions-remote uses claude --remote-control (genuine
Claude-specific feature per audit spec S9 exception clause; not modified)
---
 GENO.md                            | 2 ++
 SKILL.md                           | 1 +
 skills/geno-dev-prs-check/SKILL.md | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/GENO.md b/GENO.md
index 28d5e79..89ae88c 100644
--- a/GENO.md
+++ b/GENO.md
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ Developer and infrastructure skills for AI coding agents: task execution from la
 | geno-dev-feature-ship | feature-ship | /geno-dev-feature-ship |
 | geno-dev-issue-work | issue-work | /geno-dev-issue-work |
 | geno-dev-skills-retro | meta | /geno-dev-skills-retro |
+| geno-dev-sessions-remote | sessions | /geno-dev-sessions-remote |
 
 ## Repo structure
 
@@ -77,3 +78,4 @@ Pure markdown skillset — no Python package, no venv, no scripts. Each skill is
 - This skill never modifies a project's `.gitignore` or tracked config files.
 - **Prefix aliasing**: Slash commands use the canonical `geno-` prefix in source (e.g., `/geno-dev-tasks-start`). Short `/gt-` aliases are configured per-install by geno-tools and are not part of the skill source.
 - **Adding a new skill**: Create a directory under `skills/` named after the skill, add a `SKILL.md` with valid frontmatter (name, description, argument-hint, license, metadata), then register the skill in the skills table and repo structure tree in this file.
+- **Versioning**: `genotools.yaml` is the canonical version source. Keep `package.json` `version` and root `SKILL.md` `metadata.version` in sync with it. Bump the version whenever skills are added, removed, or behavior changes.
diff --git a/SKILL.md b/SKILL.md
index 86e6752..0e23f1d 100644
